# e2e-deslop — repo-wide architecture-deepening scan (Cursor runtime)

When the user invokes e2e-deslop ("de-slop", "deslop", "/e2e-deslop", "architecture scan", "scan for tech debt", "find refactor candidates", "architecture deepening"), follow the flow defined in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) → `.agents/skills/e2e-deslop/SKILL.md`.

**Cursor runtime constraints:**

- Scouts are read-only; no worktree fan-out is needed. Step 0 capability probe requires `spawn_agent` to dispatch one architecture-scout per eligible area. If agent spawn is unavailable, Step 0 emits `<e2e-stall reason="fanout-unavailable" />` and exits — never falls back to inline area analysis.
- If parallel slots are constrained, scouts run in bounded batches; the scan is still incremental via the scan ledger.

For full-fidelity parallel execution, the Claude Code skill version is available: `npx e2e-engineering init --target claude`.
